  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-IP24-IRQ901</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Employment policies formulated in Iraq, using strengthened LMI systems and LM statistics</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ILO partnering with the Central Statistical Organization (CSO) and Kurdistan Statistical Organization (KRSO) in Iraq, has been able to implement and publish the first national Labour Force Survey (LFS) in a decade. The survey depicts the employment&#x2019;s challenges, with a focus on the youth population. The labour market is characterized by high rates of unemployment with significant differences by age and gender. In addition, underemployment is a significant challenge to the country. In turn, a high proportion of workers are in the public sector, while informal employment dominates in the private sector. These situations exacerbate the country&#x2019;s stagnant growth, inequalities, and social challenges which necessitates to formulation of a new evidence-based National Employment Policy (NEP).
The ILO in collaboration with NEP Drafting Committee formed by the Ministry of Social Affairs and Labour (MOSAL) and its tripartite constituents and relevant stakeholders including the Parliament, has been working closely to develop the National Employment Policy for Iraq based on the findings of the LFS and informality diagnostic studies. 
In this biennium, work will focus on providing technical support for the tripartite plus discussions of the policy in the Drafting Committee and later on in the Higher Committee for Labour Force Planning, in preparation for it to be sent to the Cabinet for adoption. The support will involve providing best practice, benchmarks and innovative policy instruments that have proven effective in addressing the labour market issues that Iraq faces.</narrative>
  </description>
